<title>CHINA: China Xinjiang gold output up 20.84 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>China Xinjiang gold output up 20.84 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold output at China's northwestern region of Xinjiang rose by 20.84 percent in 1996 from the year earlier, the Economic Information Daily said on Friday.</p>
<p>It did not give a figure for the amount of gold produced.</p>
<p>The resource-rich region's gold production generated more than 75 million yuan ($9.0 million) in profits last year, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It produced six tonnes of gold in 1995 and was expected to produce 250,000 ounces of gold in the year 2000, official figures show.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
